In fintech systems, testing is not just “unit tests” — it’s about ensuring end-to-end reliability across distributed services.

1️⃣ Why Testing is Hard in Microservices?

In your system:

API Gateway → Auth → Account → Transaction → Kafka → Notification

👉 Problems:

Multiple services

Network calls

Async communication (Kafka)

Different databases

👉 So we need a layered testing strategy

2️⃣ Types of Testing (Very Important)
🔹 1. Unit Testing (Foundation)

Test individual classes

✔ Fast
✔ No DB / no network

Example
@ExtendWith(MockitoExtension.class)
class AccountServiceTest {

    @Mock
    private AccountRepository repository;

    @InjectMocks
    private AccountService service;

    @Test
    void shouldCreditAmount() {
        AccountEntity account = new AccountEntity();
        account.setBalance(BigDecimal.valueOf(100));

        when(repository.findById(1L)).thenReturn(Optional.of(account));

        service.credit(1L, BigDecimal.valueOf(50));

        assertEquals(BigDecimal.valueOf(150), account.getBalance());
    }
}
🔹 2. Integration Testing

Test:

✔ Service + DB
✔ Repository + JPA

Example
@SpringBootTest
@AutoConfigureTestDatabase
class AccountRepositoryTest {

    @Autowired
    private AccountRepository repository;

    @Test
    void testSaveAccount() {
        AccountEntity acc = new AccountEntity();
        acc.setBalance(BigDecimal.valueOf(100));

        AccountEntity saved = repository.save(acc);

        assertNotNull(saved.getId());
    }
}
🔹 3. API Testing (Controller Layer)

Test REST endpoints

@SpringBootTest
@AutoConfigureMockMvc
class AccountControllerTest {

    @Autowired
    private MockMvc mockMvc;

    @Test
    void testGetAccount() throws Exception {
        mockMvc.perform(get("/accounts/1"))
               .andExpect(status().isOk());
    }
}
🔹 4. Contract Testing (VERY IMPORTANT 🔥)

👉 Ensures:

Producer (Account Service)
Consumer (Transaction Service)

👉 Both agree on API contract

Tools:

Spring Cloud Contract

🔹 5. End-to-End Testing

Test full flow:

Transfer API → Debit → Credit → Kafka → Notification

✔ Real environment
❌ Slow

🔹 6. Kafka Testing (Async Testing)
Embedded Kafka Example
@EmbeddedKafka(partitions = 1, topics = {"transaction-events"})
@SpringBootTest
class KafkaTest {

    @Autowired
    private KafkaTemplate<String, String> kafkaTemplate;

    @Test
    void testKafkaSend() {
        kafkaTemplate.send("transaction-events", "test-event");
    }
}
