6️⃣ Testcontainers (Production-Level Testing 🔥)

Instead of fake DB:

👉 Use real DB in Docker

Example
@Testcontainers
@SpringBootTest
class MySQLTest {

    @Container
    static MySQLContainer<?> mysql =
        new MySQLContainer<>("mysql:8");

}

✔ Realistic testing
✔ Used in companies

7️⃣ Common Scenarios You MUST Test
🔹 Success Case

✔ Transfer successful

🔹 Failure Case

✔ Insufficient balance
✔ Service down

🔹 Retry Case

✔ Kafka retry works

🔹 DLQ Case

✔ Message goes to DLQ

8️⃣ CI/CD Integration

Before code merge:

✔ Run unit tests
✔ Run integration tests
✔ Check coverage (JaCoCo)

9️⃣ Coverage Goals
Unit tests → 70–80%
Critical logic → 90%+
🔟 Common Mistakes

❌ Only unit testing
❌ No Kafka testing
❌ No failure scenario testing
❌ Ignoring contract testing

1️⃣1️⃣ Interview Answer (🔥)

👉 “How do you test microservices?”

We follow a layered testing approach with unit tests for business logic,
integration tests for database interactions, contract testing for service communication,
and end-to-end testing for critical flows. We also test Kafka consumers using embedded Kafka.
🚀 Your System Now
Unit Tests → Service logic
Integration Tests → DB + JPA
API Tests → Controllers
